NOTHING WORKS WITHOUT Model Builder


NEVER test in workspace used to create a module

Use bin/project-setup --copy-module gdb-remote
Edit source
gcc 13 or higher to make

Remove the external_connection_attributes registration and function from the modules simics_start.py.

    For Simics 6
    In your project folder you must create, if it doesn't already exist, a config-user.mk file and add the following line to it, then clean/rebuild your modules.
    export SIGN_ON_BUILD=yes

    For Simics 7
       simics> enable-sign-on-build

       The resulting files can be copied to a free Simics7 workspace to create a signed package

Creating packages
parent of the workspace must have a link to SIMDIR/scripts
and to SIMDIR/linux64

use bin/project-packager with no options.  no need for a json or any other file.  That creates an ispm file

Clean the local workspace using something like:

    rm -f linux64/lib/gdb-remote.so
    rm -fr linux64/lib/python-py3/simmod/gdb_remote
    rm -fr linux64/obj/modules/gdb_remote


To install the package, go to the parent of the SIMDIR directory and use something like:
../intel-simics-package-manager-1.17.0/ispm install /eems_images/ubuntu_img/simics6/victron7/simics-pkg-200000-7.0.0-linux64.ispm -y --verbose --trust-insecure-packages
../intel-simics-package-manager-1.17.0/ispm install /tmp/simics-pkg-200000-7.0.0-linux64.ispm -y --verbose --trust-insecure-packages

bin/addon-manager -h
bin/addon-manager -s /mnt/resim_eems/resim/archive/simics7_wr/install/simics-resim-gdb-7.0.0


That would over-ride the stock gdb-remote

Uninstall the package:
   ../intel-simics-package-manager-1.17.0/ispm uninstall 200000-7.0.0
